{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788341431178,"sessionID":"ses_f9e8d1600ffeTOnADKxO6TVRTr","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_73a4d359727041958142327d","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/aloschilov/workspace/pyasc-skill-stack/skills/pyasc-codegen-workflow/templates/design-template.md"},"output":"<path>/home/aloschilov/workspace/pyasc-skill-stack/skills/pyasc-codegen-workflow/templates/design-template.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Kernel Design: {kernel_name}\n2: \n3: ## 1. Operation description\n4: \n5: **Mathematical definition**: {describe the operation, e.g., out = x + y}\n6: \n7: **Input tensors**: {list input tensors with shapes and dtypes}\n8: \n9: **Output tensors**: {list output tensors with shapes and dtypes}\n10: \n11: ## 2. pyasc API selection\n12: \n13: | Purpose | API | Module |\n14: |---------|-----|--------|\n15: | Kernel decorator | `@asc2.jit(always_compile=True)` | `asc2` |\n16: | Global memory wrapper | `asc2.tensor(ptr, [shape])` | `asc2` |\n17: | Load tile from GM | `asc2.load(gm, [tile_shape], offsets=[...])` | `asc2` |\n18: | Store tile to GM | `asc2.store(tile, gm, offsets=[...])` | `asc2` |\n19: | Tile loop | `asc2.range(n)` | `asc2` |\n20: | Block index | `asc2.block_idx()` | `asc2` |\n21: | Computation | {e.g., `x + y` or `asc2.abs(x)`} | `asc2` / operators |\n22: | Kernel params | `asc.GlobalAddress`, `asc.ConstExpr[int]` | `asc` |\n23: | Tiling math | `asc.ceildiv(a, b)` | `asc` |\n24: \n25: ## 3. Multi-core strategy\n26: \n27: - **Core count**: {e.g., 16}\n28: - **Tile size**: {e.g., 128 elements}\n29: - **Tiles per block**: `asc.ceildiv(num_tiles, core_num)`\n30: - **Work distribution**: Each core processes `tile_per_block` tiles starting from `block_idx() * tile_size * tile_per_block`\n31: \n32: ## 4. Verification plan\n33: \n34: - **Backend**: Model (simulator) and/or NPU\n35: - **Reference**: {e.g., numpy x + y}\n36: - **Tolerance**: {e.g., atol=1e-5, rtol=1e-5}\n37: - **Test sizes**: {list of sizes to test}\n38: \n39: ## 5. Syntax compliance check\n40: \n41: - [ ] All constructs inside `@asc2.jit` are in the supported set\n42: - [ ] No unsupported syntax (print, break, continue, lambda, etc.)\n43: - [ ] Kernel does not return a value\n44: - [ ] All device function returns are top-level only\n45: - [ ] Variables initialized before conditional use\n\n(End of file - total 45 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Kernel Design: {kernel_name}\n\n## 1. Operation description\n\n**Mathematical definition**: {describe the operation, e.g., out = x + y}\n\n**Input tensors**: {list input tensors with shapes and dtypes}\n\n**Output tensors**: {list output tensors with shapes and dtypes}\n\n## 2. pyasc API selection\n\n| Purpose | API | Module |\n|---------|-----|--------|\n| Kernel decorator | `@asc2.jit(always_compile=True)` | `asc2` |\n| Global memory wrapper | `asc2.tensor(ptr, [shape])` | `asc2` |\n| Load tile from GM | `asc2.load(gm, [tile_shape], offsets=[...])` | `asc2` |\n| Store tile to GM | `asc2.store(tile, gm, offsets=[...])` | `asc2` |\n| Tile loop | `asc2.range(n)` | `asc2` |\n| Block index | `asc2.block_idx()` | `asc2` |","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/home/aloschilov/workspace/pyasc-skill-stack/skills/pyasc-codegen-workflow/templates/design-template.md","text":"# Kernel Design: {kernel_name}\n\n## 1. Operation description\n\n**Mathematical definition**: {describe the operation, e.g., out = x + y}\n\n**Input tensors**: {list input tensors with shapes and dtypes}\n\n**Output tensors**: {list output tensors with shapes and dtypes}\n\n## 2. pyasc API selection\n\n| Purpose | API | Module |\n|---------|-----|--------|\n| Kernel decorator | `@asc2.jit(always_compile=True)` | `asc2` |\n| Global memory wrapper | `asc2.tensor(ptr, [shape])` | `asc2` |\n| Load tile from GM | `asc2.load(gm, [tile_shape], offsets=[...])` | `asc2` |\n| Store tile to GM | `asc2.store(tile, gm, offsets=[...])` | `asc2` |\n| Tile loop | `asc2.range(n)` | `asc2` |\n| Block index | `asc2.block_idx()` | `asc2` |\n| Computation | {e.g., `x + y` or `asc2.abs(x)`} | `asc2` / operators |\n| Kernel params | `asc.GlobalAddress`, `asc.ConstExpr[int]` | `asc` |\n| Tiling math | `asc.ceildiv(a, b)` | `asc` |\n\n## 3. Multi-core strategy\n\n- **Core count**: {e.g., 16}\n- **Tile size**: {e.g., 128 elements}\n- **Tiles per block**: `asc.ceildiv(num_tiles, core_num)`\n- **Work distribution**: Each core processes `tile_per_block` tiles starting from `block_idx() * tile_size * tile_per_block`\n\n## 4. Verification plan\n\n- **Backend**: Model (simulator) and/or NPU\n- **Reference**: {e.g., numpy x + y}\n- **Tolerance**: {e.g., atol=1e-5, rtol=1e-5}\n- **Test sizes**: {list of sizes to test}\n\n## 5. Syntax compliance check\n\n- [ ] All constructs inside `@asc2.jit` are in the supported set\n- [ ] No unsupported syntax (print, break, continue, lambda, etc.)\n- [ ] Kernel does not return a value\n- [ ] All device function returns are top-level only\n- [ ] Variables initialized before conditional use","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":45,"totalLines":45,"truncated":false}},"title":"skills/pyasc-codegen-workflow/templates/design-template.md","time":{"start":1788341431170,"end":1788341431176}},"id":"prt_06174aa500012i17xw556XQnGy","sessionID":"ses_f9e8d1600ffeTOnADKxO6TVRTr","messageID":"msg_061731270001jmLm0nEc2v35wc"}}
