{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788341821562,"sessionID":"ses_f9e8d1600ffeTOnADKxO6TVRTr","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_ea124d9c027b4a578d892113","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/aloschilov/workspace/pyasc-skill-stack/golden/kernels/rms_norm_f32.py"},"output":"<path>/home/aloschilov/workspace/pyasc-skill-stack/golden/kernels/rms_norm_f32.py</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: #!/usr/bin/env python3.10\n2: \"\"\"Golden kernel: rms_norm/float32\n3: \n4: Two-variant RMSNorm with a host-side dispatcher, mirroring the CANN\n5: arch35 (C310) ``rms_norm`` op layout in\n6: ``opp/built-in/op_impl/ai_core/tbe/impl/ops_nn/ascendc/rms_norm/rms_norm.cpp``:\n7: \n8:   - ``KernelRmsNormRegBase``      (tiling key 5000) -> full_row branch\n9:   - ``KernelRmsNormRegBaseSplitD`` (tiling key 2001) -> split_d branch\n10: \n11: Both kernels run on ``Ascend950PR_9599`` (compilation arch C310) and use\n12: ``torch.Tensor`` inputs. The dispatcher picks one kernel based on\n13: ``num_cols * dtype_bytes`` against a conservative UB budget; this\n14: matches CANN's ``TILING_KEY_IS`` switch in spirit but in pure Python.\n15: \n16: Cell metadata (mirrors capabilities.yaml; do not drift):\n17:   - shape_regime: dynamic         # full_row vs split_d via dispatcher\n18:   - reduce_axis: -1\n19:   - output_shape: same_as_input\n20:   - accumulator_dtype: float32\n21:   - identity: \"0\"\n22:   - tail_behavior: host_dispatcher\n23:   - padding: null                 # split_d uses host zero-pad to 64\n24:   - partitioning: host_dispatcher\n25:   - unsupported_regimes:\n26:       [dynamic_num_cols_not_8_aligned_in_full_row,\n27:        num_cols_below_split_d_tile_threshold]\n28:   - dispatcher_note: rms_norm_launch(x, gamma, eps) picks full_row\n29:     when num_cols * dtype_bytes <= 64KB and num_cols % 8 == 0,\n30:     otherwise split_d.\n31: \n32: Non-obvious constraints (Phase 1.5):\n33:   - Alignment: full_row requires ``num_cols % 8 == 0``; split_d\n34:     pads ``num_cols`` up to a multiple of ``tile_cols = 64`` on\n35:     the host (with zeros) and slices the output back. The\n36:     sum-of-squares divides by REAL ``num_cols`` so the padding\n37:     zeros do not bias the mean-square.\n38:   - UB/L1/L0 placement: every load lives in UB (no L0 / cube\n39:     involvement). ``full_row`` loads ``[1, num_cols]`` per row at\n40:     once; ``split_d`` loads ``[1, tile_cols=64]`` per inner-loop\n41:     iteration.\n42:   - UB budget: full_row chosen iff\n43:     ``num_cols * dtype_bytes <= 64 KiB`` (``UB_BUDGET_BYTES = 65536``);\n44:     e.g. ``256 * 4 = 1024 B`` fits comfortably, ``1055 * 4 ≈ 4 KiB``\n45:     also fits in bytes terms but the 8-alignment guard routes it\n46:     to split_d.\n47:   - Padding: null at the cell level. split_d's host zero-padding\n48:     is documented under ``tail_behavior=host_dispatcher`` — i.e.\n49:     the dispatcher itself is the tail mechanism.\n50:   - Tail behavior: ``host_dispatcher``. The dispatcher chooses\n51:     full_row when the row fits in UB and is 8-aligned, otherwise\n52:     split_d (which streams along D in 64-element tiles with host\n53:     zero-padding).\n54:   - Accumulator dtype: ``float32``.\n55:   - Reduction axis: -1.\n56:   - Identity: ``\"0\"``.\n57:   - Dispatcher choice (rms_norm only): full_row when\n58:     ``num_cols * dtype_bytes <= UB_BUDGET_BYTES`` AND\n59:     ``num_cols % 8 == 0``; otherwise split_d.\n60:   - Simulator/platform assumptions: ``Ascend950PR_9599`` (C310);\n61:     inputs MUST be ``torch.Tensor`` — numpy buffers are silently\n62:     zeroed by the C310 simulator path.\n63: \n64: Test shapes (both verified in a single ``run_kernel`` call):\n65:   - (8, 256)  exercises full_row (row tile fits in UB).\n66:   - (8, 1055) exercises split_d (row exceeds UB; host-padded to 1088).\n67: \n68: Tolerances: full_row ``atol=rtol=1e-4``, split_d ``atol=rtol=1e-4``\n69: (both well under torch.testing.assert_close defaults for f32).\n70: \"\"\"\n71: \n72: import logging\n73: import argparse\n74: import torch\n75: \n76: import asc\n77: import asc.runtime.config as config\n78: import asc2\n79: \n80: CORE_NUM = 8\n81: TILE_COLS = 64\n82: EPS = 1e-5\n83: UB_BUDGET_BYTES = 64 * 1024\n84: \n85: logging.basicConfig(level=logging.INFO)\n86: \n87: \n88: @asc2.jit(reuse_alloc=1)\n89: def rms_norm_full_row_kernel(x_ptr: asc2.GlobalAddress, gamma_ptr: asc2.GlobalAddress,\n90:                              out_ptr: asc2.GlobalAddress,\n91:                              num_rows: int,\n92:                              num_cols: asc2.ConstExpr,\n93:                              epsilon: asc.ConstExpr[float]):\n94:     \"\"\"Full-row variant. ``num_cols`` is compile-time so the row tile shape\n95:     is known. Loads ``[1, num_cols]`` per row, reduces inside the tile,\n96:     multiplies by gamma + inv_rms, stores back. Mirrors CANN's\n97:     ``KernelRmsNormRegBase``.\n98:     \"\"\"\n99:     x_gm = asc2.global_tensor(x_ptr, [num_rows, num_cols])\n100:     gamma_gm_2d = asc2.global_tensor(gamma_ptr, [1, num_cols])\n101:     out_gm = asc2.global_tensor(out_ptr, [num_rows, num_cols])\n102: \n103:     for row in asc2.range(asc2.block_idx(), num_rows, asc2.block_num(),\n104:                           unroll_factor=2):\n105:         x_row = asc2.copy_in(x_gm, [row, 0], [1, num_cols])\n106:         x_row_f32 = x_row.to(asc.float32)\n107:         sum_sq = asc2.reduce_sum(x_row_f32 * x_row_f32)\n108:         inv_rms = 1.0 / asc2.sqrt(sum_sq / num_cols + epsilon)\n109: \n110:         gamma_row = asc2.copy_in(gamma_gm_2d, [0, 0], [1, num_cols])\n111:         gamma_row_f32 = gamma_row.to(asc.float32)\n112:         out_f32 = x_row_f32 * gamma_row_f32 * inv_rms\n113:         asc2.copy_out(out_f32.to(x_row.dtype), out_gm, [row, 0])\n114: \n115: \n116: @asc2.jit(reuse_alloc=1)\n117: def rms_norm_split_d_kernel(x_ptr: asc2.GlobalAddress, gamma_ptr: asc2.GlobalAddress,\n118:                             out_ptr: asc2.GlobalAddress,\n119:                             num_rows: int, num_cols: int, padded_cols: int,\n120:                             num_tiles: int,\n121:                             tile_cols: asc2.ConstExpr,\n122:                             epsilon: asc.ConstExpr[float]):\n123:     \"\"\"Split-D variant. Both ``num_rows`` and ``num_cols`` are runtime int.\n124:     Streams along D in ``tile_cols=64`` (one Ascend SIMD lane) tiles; the\n125:     host pre-pads ``x``/``gamma`` to a multiple of ``tile_cols`` and slices\n126:     the output back. ``sum_sq`` is divided by REAL ``num_cols``, so padded\n127:     zeros do not bias the mean-square. Mirrors CANN's\n128:     ``KernelRmsNormRegBaseSplitD``.\n129:     \"\"\"\n130:     x_gm = asc2.global_tensor(x_ptr, [num_rows, padded_cols])\n131:     gamma_gm_2d = asc2.global_tensor(gamma_ptr, [1, padded_cols])\n132:     out_gm = asc2.global_tensor(out_ptr, [num_rows, padded_cols])\n133: \n134:     for row in asc2.range(asc2.block_idx(), num_rows, asc2.block_num(),\n135:                           unroll_factor=2):\n136:         zero_seed = asc2.full([1, tile_cols], 0.0, dtype=asc.float32)\n137:         sum_sq = asc2.reduce_sum(zero_seed)\n138: \n139:         # Inner reduction loop carries `sum_sq` across iterations -> NOT parallel.\n140:         for tile_id in asc2.range(num_tiles, unroll_factor=2):\n141:             col = tile_id * tile_cols\n142:             x = asc2.copy_in(x_gm, [row, col], [1, tile_cols])\n143:             x_f32 = x.to(asc.float32)\n144:             sum_sq = sum_sq + asc2.reduce_sum(x_f32 * x_f32)\n145: \n146:         inv_rms = 1.0 / asc2.sqrt(sum_sq / num_cols + epsilon)\n147: \n148:         # Disjoint write-back -> safe to parallelise.\n149:         for tile_id in asc2.range(num_tiles, unroll_factor=2):\n150:             col = tile_id * tile_cols\n151:             x = asc2.copy_in(x_gm, [row, col], [1, tile_cols])\n152:             gamma = asc2.copy_in(gamma_gm_2d, [0, col], [1, tile_cols])\n153:             x_f32 = x.to(asc.float32)\n154:             gamma_f32 = gamma.to(asc.float32)\n155:             out_f32 = x_f32 * gamma_f32 * inv_rms\n156:             asc2.copy_out(out_f32.to(x.dtype), out_gm, [row, col])\n157: \n158: \n159: def _full_row_launch(x: torch.Tensor, gamma: torch.Tensor, eps: float,\n160:                      core_num: int) -> torch.Tensor:\n161:     num_rows, num_cols = x.shape\n162:     out = torch.empty_like(x)\n163:     rms_norm_full_row_kernel[core_num](x, gamma, out, num_rows, num_cols, eps)\n164:     return out\n165: \n166: \n167: def _split_d_launch(x: torch.Tensor, gamma: torch.Tensor, eps: float,\n168:                     core_num: int, tile_cols: int = TILE_COLS) -> torch.Tensor:\n169:     num_rows, num_cols = x.shape\n170:     padded_cols = ((num_cols + tile_cols - 1) // tile_cols) * tile_cols\n171: \n172:     if padded_cols == num_cols:\n173:         x_padded = x\n174:         gamma_padded = gamma\n175:     else:\n176:         x_padded = torch.zeros((num_rows, padded_cols), dtype=x.dtype)\n177:         x_padded[:, :num_cols] = x\n178:         gamma_padded = torch.zeros((padded_cols,), dtype=gamma.dtype)\n179:         gamma_padded[:num_cols] = gamma\n180: \n181:     out_padded = torch.zeros((num_rows, padded_cols), dtype=x.dtype)\n182:     num_tiles = padded_cols // tile_cols\n183:     rms_norm_split_d_kernel[core_num](x_padded, gamma_padded, out_padded,\n184:                                       num_rows, num_cols, padded_cols,\n185:                                       num_tiles, tile_cols, eps)\n186:     return out_padded[:, :num_cols].clone()\n187: \n188: \n189: def rms_norm_launch(x: torch.Tensor, gamma: torch.Tensor,\n190:                     eps: float = EPS,\n191:                     core_num: int = CORE_NUM) -> torch.Tensor:\n192:     \"\"\"Host-side dispatcher between the two C310 variants.\n193: \n194:     The threshold mirrors CANN's tiling: when one row fits in UB with\n195:     headroom for accumulator, gamma, and double-buffer, use the full-row\n196:     kernel (faster). Otherwise stream along D.\n197:     \"\"\"\n198:     num_rows, num_cols = x.shape\n199:     dtype_bytes = x.element_size()\n200:     row_bytes = num_cols * dtype_bytes\n201:     if row_bytes <= UB_BUDGET_BYTES and num_cols % 8 == 0:\n202:         return _full_row_launch(x, gamma, eps, core_num)\n203:     return _split_d_launch(x, gamma, eps, core_num)\n204: \n205: \n206: def torch_rms_norm(x: torch.Tensor, gamma: torch.Tensor, eps: float) -> torch.Tensor:\n207:     x32 = x.to(torch.float32)\n208:     mean_sq = torch.mean(x32 * x32, dim=-1, keepdim=True)\n209:     return (x32 * torch.rsqrt(mean_sq + eps) * gamma.to(torch.float32)).to(x.dtype)\n210: \n211: \n212: def run_kernel(backend: config.Backend, platform: config.Platform):\n213:     config.set_platform(backend, platform)\n214: \n215:     rng = torch.Generator().manual_seed(2026)\n216: \n217:     num_rows, num_cols = 8, 256\n218:     x = torch.randn((num_rows, num_cols), generator=rng, dtype=torch.float32)\n219:     gamma = torch.randn((num_cols,), generator=rng, dtype=torch.float32)\n220:     out = rms_norm_launch(x, gamma, EPS)\n221:     expected = torch_rms_norm(x, gamma, EPS)\n222:     torch.testing.assert_close(out, expected, atol=1e-4, rtol=1e-4)\n223:     logging.info(f\"[PASS] full_row branch shape ({num_rows}, {num_cols})\")\n224: \n225:     num_rows, num_cols = 8, 1055\n226:     x = torch.randn((num_rows, num_cols), generator=rng, dtype=torch.float32)\n227:     gamma = torch.randn((num_cols,), generator=rng, dtype=torch.float32)\n228:     out = rms_norm_launch(x, gamma, EPS)\n229:     expected = torch_rms_norm(x, gamma, EPS)\n230:     torch.testing.assert_close(out, expected, atol=1e-4, rtol=1e-4)\n231:     logging.info(f\"[PASS] split_d branch shape ({num_rows}, {num_cols})\")\n232: \n233: \n234: def test_rms_norm_f32(backend: config.Backend, platform: config.Platform):\n235:     \"\"\"pytest entry point.\"\"\"\n236:     run_kernel(backend, platform)\n237: \n238: \n239: if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n240:     parser = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n241:     parser.add_argument(\"-r\", type=str, default=\"Model\", help=\"backend: Model or NPU\")\n242:     parser.add_argument(\"-v\", type=str, default=\"Ascend950PR_9599\",\n243:                         help=\"platform/SoC version (RMSNorm requires C310)\")\n244:     args = parser.parse_args()\n245:     backend = args.r\n246:     platform = args.v\n247:     if backend not in config.Backend.__members__:\n248:         raise ValueError(f\"Unsupported Backend! Supported: {list(config.Backend.__members__.keys())}\")\n249:     backend = config.Backend(backend)\n250:     if platform is not None:\n251:         platform_values = [p.value for p in config.Platform]\n252:         if platform not in platform_values:\n253:             raise ValueError(f\"Unsupported Platform! Supported: {platform_values}\")\n254:         platform = config.Platform(platform)\n255:     logging.info(f\"[INFO] Running kernel with backend={backend}, platform={platform}\")\n256:     run_kernel(backend, platform)\n257:     logging.info(\"[INFO] Kernel run complete.\")\n\n(End of file - total 257 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"#!/usr/bin/env python3.10\n\"\"\"Golden kernel: rms_norm/float32\n\nTwo-variant RMSNorm with a host-side dispatcher, mirroring the CANN\narch35 (C310) ``rms_norm`` op layout in\n``opp/built-in/op_impl/ai_core/tbe/impl/ops_nn/ascendc/rms_norm/rms_norm.cpp``:\n\n  - ``KernelRmsNormRegBase``      (tiling key 5000) -> full_row branch\n  - ``KernelRmsNormRegBaseSplitD`` (tiling key 2001) -> split_d branch\n\nBoth kernels run on ``Ascend950PR_9599`` (compilation arch C310) and use\n``torch.Tensor`` inputs. The dispatcher picks one kernel based on\n``num_cols * dtype_bytes`` against a conservative UB budget; this\nmatches CANN's ``TILING_KEY_IS`` switch in spirit but in pure Python.\n\nCell metadata (mirrors capabilities.yaml; do not drift):\n  - shape_regime: dynamic         # full_row vs split_d via dispatcher\n  - reduce_axis: -1\n  - output_shape: same_as_input\n  - accumulator_dtype: float32","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/home/aloschilov/workspace/pyasc-skill-stack/golden/kernels/rms_norm_f32.py","text":"#!/usr/bin/env python3.10\n\"\"\"Golden kernel: rms_norm/float32\n\nTwo-variant RMSNorm with a host-side dispatcher, mirroring the CANN\narch35 (C310) ``rms_norm`` op layout in\n``opp/built-in/op_impl/ai_core/tbe/impl/ops_nn/ascendc/rms_norm/rms_norm.cpp``:\n\n  - ``KernelRmsNormRegBase``      (tiling key 5000) -> full_row branch\n  - ``KernelRmsNormRegBaseSplitD`` (tiling key 2001) -> split_d branch\n\nBoth kernels run on ``Ascend950PR_9599`` (compilation arch C310) and use\n``torch.Tensor`` inputs. The dispatcher picks one kernel based on\n``num_cols * dtype_bytes`` against a conservative UB budget; this\nmatches CANN's ``TILING_KEY_IS`` switch in spirit but in pure Python.\n\nCell metadata (mirrors capabilities.yaml; do not drift):\n  - shape_regime: dynamic         # full_row vs split_d via dispatcher\n  - reduce_axis: -1\n  - output_shape: same_as_input\n  - accumulator_dtype: float32\n  - identity: \"0\"\n  - tail_behavior: host_dispatcher\n  - padding: null                 # split_d uses host zero-pad to 64\n  - partitioning: host_dispatcher\n  - unsupported_regimes:\n      [dynamic_num_cols_not_8_aligned_in_full_row,\n       num_cols_below_split_d_tile_threshold]\n  - dispatcher_note: rms_norm_launch(x, gamma, eps) picks full_row\n    when num_cols * dtype_bytes <= 64KB and num_cols % 8 == 0,\n    otherwise split_d.\n\nNon-obvious constraints (Phase 1.5):\n  - Alignment: full_row requires ``num_cols % 8 == 0``; split_d\n    pads ``num_cols`` up to a multiple of ``tile_cols = 64`` on\n    the host (with zeros) and slices the output back. The\n    sum-of-squares divides by REAL ``num_cols`` so the padding\n    zeros do not bias the mean-square.\n  - UB/L1/L0 placement: every load lives in UB (no L0 / cube\n    involvement). ``full_row`` loads ``[1, num_cols]`` per row at\n    once; ``split_d`` loads ``[1, tile_cols=64]`` per inner-loop\n    iteration.\n  - UB budget: full_row chosen iff\n    ``num_cols * dtype_bytes <= 64 KiB`` (``UB_BUDGET_BYTES = 65536``);\n    e.g. ``256 * 4 = 1024 B`` fits comfortably, ``1055 * 4 ≈ 4 KiB``\n    also fits in bytes terms but the 8-alignment guard routes it\n    to split_d.\n  - Padding: null at the cell level. split_d's host zero-padding\n    is documented under ``tail_behavior=host_dispatcher`` — i.e.\n    the dispatcher itself is the tail mechanism.\n  - Tail behavior: ``host_dispatcher``. The dispatcher chooses\n    full_row when the row fits in UB and is 8-aligned, otherwise\n    split_d (which streams along D in 64-element tiles with host\n    zero-padding).\n  - Accumulator dtype: ``float32``.\n  - Reduction axis: -1.\n  - Identity: ``\"0\"``.\n  - Dispatcher choice (rms_norm only): full_row when\n    ``num_cols * dtype_bytes <= UB_BUDGET_BYTES`` AND\n    ``num_cols % 8 == 0``; otherwise split_d.\n  - Simulator/platform assumptions: ``Ascend950PR_9599`` (C310);\n    inputs MUST be ``torch.Tensor`` — numpy buffers are silently\n    zeroed by the C310 simulator path.\n\nTest shapes (both verified in a single ``run_kernel`` call):\n  - (8, 256)  exercises full_row (row tile fits in UB).\n  - (8, 1055) exercises split_d (row exceeds UB; host-padded to 1088).\n\nTolerances: full_row ``atol=rtol=1e-4``, split_d ``atol=rtol=1e-4``\n(both well under torch.testing.assert_close defaults for f32).\n\"\"\"\n\nimport logging\nimport argparse\nimport torch\n\nimport asc\nimport asc.runtime.config as config\nimport asc2\n\nCORE_NUM = 8\nTILE_COLS = 64\nEPS = 1e-5\nUB_BUDGET_BYTES = 64 * 1024\n\nlogging.basicConfig(level=logging.INFO)\n\n\n@asc2.jit(reuse_alloc=1)\ndef rms_norm_full_row_kernel(x_ptr: asc2.GlobalAddress, gamma_ptr: asc2.GlobalAddress,\n                             out_ptr: asc2.GlobalAddress,\n                             num_rows: int,\n                             num_cols: asc2.ConstExpr,\n                             epsilon: asc.ConstExpr[float]):\n    \"\"\"Full-row variant. ``num_cols`` is compile-time so the row tile shape\n    is known. Loads ``[1, num_cols]`` per row, reduces inside the tile,\n    multiplies by gamma + inv_rms, stores back. Mirrors CANN's\n    ``KernelRmsNormRegBase``.\n    \"\"\"\n    x_gm = asc2.global_tensor(x_ptr, [num_rows, num_cols])\n    gamma_gm_2d = asc2.global_tensor(gamma_ptr, [1, num_cols])\n    out_gm = asc2.global_tensor(out_ptr, [num_rows, num_cols])\n\n    for row in asc2.range(asc2.block_idx(), num_rows, asc2.block_num(),\n                          unroll_factor=2):\n        x_row = asc2.copy_in(x_gm, [row, 0], [1, num_cols])\n        x_row_f32 = x_row.to(asc.float32)\n        sum_sq = asc2.reduce_sum(x_row_f32 * x_row_f32)\n        inv_rms = 1.0 / asc2.sqrt(sum_sq / num_cols + epsilon)\n\n        gamma_row = asc2.copy_in(gamma_gm_2d, [0, 0], [1, num_cols])\n        gamma_row_f32 = gamma_row.to(asc.float32)\n        out_f32 = x_row_f32 * gamma_row_f32 * inv_rms\n        asc2.copy_out(out_f32.to(x_row.dtype), out_gm, [row, 0])\n\n\n@asc2.jit(reuse_alloc=1)\ndef rms_norm_split_d_kernel(x_ptr: asc2.GlobalAddress, gamma_ptr: asc2.GlobalAddress,\n                            out_ptr: asc2.GlobalAddress,\n                            num_rows: int, num_cols: int, padded_cols: int,\n                            num_tiles: int,\n                            tile_cols: asc2.ConstExpr,\n                            epsilon: asc.ConstExpr[float]):\n    \"\"\"Split-D variant. Both ``num_rows`` and ``num_cols`` are runtime int.\n    Streams along D in ``tile_cols=64`` (one Ascend SIMD lane) tiles; the\n    host pre-pads ``x``/``gamma`` to a multiple of ``tile_cols`` and slices\n    the output back. ``sum_sq`` is divided by REAL ``num_cols``, so padded\n    zeros do not bias the mean-square. Mirrors CANN's\n    ``KernelRmsNormRegBaseSplitD``.\n    \"\"\"\n    x_gm = asc2.global_tensor(x_ptr, [num_rows, padded_cols])\n    gamma_gm_2d = asc2.global_tensor(gamma_ptr, [1, padded_cols])\n    out_gm = asc2.global_tensor(out_ptr, [num_rows, padded_cols])\n\n    for row in asc2.range(asc2.block_idx(), num_rows, asc2.block_num(),\n                          unroll_factor=2):\n        zero_seed = asc2.full([1, tile_cols], 0.0, dtype=asc.float32)\n        sum_sq = asc2.reduce_sum(zero_seed)\n\n        # Inner reduction loop carries `sum_sq` across iterations -> NOT parallel.\n        for tile_id in asc2.range(num_tiles, unroll_factor=2):\n            col = tile_id * tile_cols\n            x = asc2.copy_in(x_gm, [row, col], [1, tile_cols])\n            x_f32 = x.to(asc.float32)\n            sum_sq = sum_sq + asc2.reduce_sum(x_f32 * x_f32)\n\n        inv_rms = 1.0 / asc2.sqrt(sum_sq / num_cols + epsilon)\n\n        # Disjoint write-back -> safe to parallelise.\n        for tile_id in asc2.range(num_tiles, unroll_factor=2):\n            col = tile_id * tile_cols\n            x = asc2.copy_in(x_gm, [row, col], [1, tile_cols])\n            gamma = asc2.copy_in(gamma_gm_2d, [0, col], [1, tile_cols])\n            x_f32 = x.to(asc.float32)\n            gamma_f32 = gamma.to(asc.float32)\n            out_f32 = x_f32 * gamma_f32 * inv_rms\n            asc2.copy_out(out_f32.to(x.dtype), out_gm, [row, col])\n\n\ndef _full_row_launch(x: torch.Tensor, gamma: torch.Tensor, eps: float,\n                     core_num: int) -> torch.Tensor:\n    num_rows, num_cols = x.shape\n    out = torch.empty_like(x)\n    rms_norm_full_row_kernel[core_num](x, gamma, out, num_rows, num_cols, eps)\n    return out\n\n\ndef _split_d_launch(x: torch.Tensor, gamma: torch.Tensor, eps: float,\n                    core_num: int, tile_cols: int = TILE_COLS) -> torch.Tensor:\n    num_rows, num_cols = x.shape\n    padded_cols = ((num_cols + tile_cols - 1) // tile_cols) * tile_cols\n\n    if padded_cols == num_cols:\n        x_padded = x\n        gamma_padded = gamma\n    else:\n        x_padded = torch.zeros((num_rows, padded_cols), dtype=x.dtype)\n        x_padded[:, :num_cols] = x\n        gamma_padded = torch.zeros((padded_cols,), dtype=gamma.dtype)\n        gamma_padded[:num_cols] = gamma\n\n    out_padded = torch.zeros((num_rows, padded_cols), dtype=x.dtype)\n    num_tiles = padded_cols // tile_cols\n    rms_norm_split_d_kernel[core_num](x_padded, gamma_padded, out_padded,\n                                      num_rows, num_cols, padded_cols,\n                                      num_tiles, tile_cols, eps)\n    return out_padded[:, :num_cols].clone()\n\n\ndef rms_norm_launch(x: torch.Tensor, gamma: torch.Tensor,\n                    eps: float = EPS,\n                    core_num: int = CORE_NUM) -> torch.Tensor:\n    \"\"\"Host-side dispatcher between the two C310 variants.\n\n    The threshold mirrors CANN's tiling: when one row fits in UB with\n    headroom for accumulator, gamma, and double-buffer, use the full-row\n    kernel (faster). Otherwise stream along D.\n    \"\"\"\n    num_rows, num_cols = x.shape\n    dtype_bytes = x.element_size()\n    row_bytes = num_cols * dtype_bytes\n    if row_bytes <= UB_BUDGET_BYTES and num_cols % 8 == 0:\n        return _full_row_launch(x, gamma, eps, core_num)\n    return _split_d_launch(x, gamma, eps, core_num)\n\n\ndef torch_rms_norm(x: torch.Tensor, gamma: torch.Tensor, eps: float) -> torch.Tensor:\n    x32 = x.to(torch.float32)\n    mean_sq = torch.mean(x32 * x32, dim=-1, keepdim=True)\n    return (x32 * torch.rsqrt(mean_sq + eps) * gamma.to(torch.float32)).to(x.dtype)\n\n\ndef run_kernel(backend: config.Backend, platform: config.Platform):\n    config.set_platform(backend, platform)\n\n    rng = torch.Generator().manual_seed(2026)\n\n    num_rows, num_cols = 8, 256\n    x = torch.randn((num_rows, num_cols), generator=rng, dtype=torch.float32)\n    gamma = torch.randn((num_cols,), generator=rng, dtype=torch.float32)\n    out = rms_norm_launch(x, gamma, EPS)\n    expected = torch_rms_norm(x, gamma, EPS)\n    torch.testing.assert_close(out, expected, atol=1e-4, rtol=1e-4)\n    logging.info(f\"[PASS] full_row branch shape ({num_rows}, {num_cols})\")\n\n    num_rows, num_cols = 8, 1055\n    x = torch.randn((num_rows, num_cols), generator=rng, dtype=torch.float32)\n    gamma = torch.randn((num_cols,), generator=rng, dtype=torch.float32)\n    out = rms_norm_launch(x, gamma, EPS)\n    expected = torch_rms_norm(x, gamma, EPS)\n    torch.testing.assert_close(out, expected, atol=1e-4, rtol=1e-4)\n    logging.info(f\"[PASS] split_d branch shape ({num_rows}, {num_cols})\")\n\n\ndef test_rms_norm_f32(backend: config.Backend, platform: config.Platform):\n    \"\"\"pytest entry point.\"\"\"\n    run_kernel(backend, platform)\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n    parser.add_argument(\"-r\", type=str, default=\"Model\", help=\"backend: Model or NPU\")\n    parser.add_argument(\"-v\", type=str, default=\"Ascend950PR_9599\",\n                        help=\"platform/SoC version (RMSNorm requires C310)\")\n    args = parser.parse_args()\n    backend = args.r\n    platform = args.v\n    if backend not in config.Backend.__members__:\n        raise ValueError(f\"Unsupported Backend! Supported: {list(config.Backend.__members__.keys())}\")\n    backend = config.Backend(backend)\n    if platform is not None:\n        platform_values = [p.value for p in config.Platform]\n        if platform not in platform_values:\n            raise ValueError(f\"Unsupported Platform! Supported: {platform_values}\")\n        platform = config.Platform(platform)\n    logging.info(f\"[INFO] Running kernel with backend={backend}, platform={platform}\")\n    run_kernel(backend, platform)\n    logging.info(\"[INFO] Kernel run complete.\")","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":257,"totalLines":257,"truncated":false}},"title":"golden/kernels/rms_norm_f32.py","time":{"start":1788341821554,"end":1788341821560}},"id":"prt_0617a9f37001tkeY9TIAgUobfk","sessionID":"ses_f9e8d1600ffeTOnADKxO6TVRTr","messageID":"msg_0617a1e5a001Nc6TkOU2dTjsR2"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788341821964,"sessionID":"ses_f9e8d1600ffeTOnADKxO6TVRTr","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_2260f5e0fba64d8b8de7103e","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/aloschilov/workspace/pyasc-skill-stack/integrations/cannbench/submission/cann_bench/rms_norm.py"},"output":"<path>/home/aloschilov/workspace/pyasc-skill-stack/integrations/cannbench/submission/cann_bench/rms_norm.py</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: \"\"\"CANN Bench RMSNorm using pyasc v2's native AscTile RMSNorm op.\"\"\"\n2: \n3: import torch\n4: \n5: import asc\n6: import asc2\n7: \n8: from ._pyasc_runtime import ensure_npu_platform\n9: \n10: _MAX_CORES = 72\n11: _MAX_TILE_ELEMENTS = 4096\n12: \n13: \n14: @asc2.jit(reuse_alloc=1)\n15: def _rms_norm_fallback_kernel(x_ptr: asc.GlobalAddress,\n16:                               gamma_ptr: asc.GlobalAddress,\n17:                               out_ptr: asc.GlobalAddress,\n18:                               rows: int,\n19:                               cols: int,\n20:                               num_tiles: int,\n21:                               tile_size: asc.ConstExpr[int],\n22:                               epsilon: float):\n23:     \"\"\"Padded two-pass fallback for unaligned D or native FP32 UB overflow.\"\"\"\n24:     x_gm = asc2.global_tensor(x_ptr, [rows, cols])\n25:     gamma_gm = asc2.global_tensor(gamma_ptr, [cols])\n26:     out_gm = asc2.global_tensor(out_ptr, [rows, cols])\n27: \n28:     for row in asc2.range(asc2.block_idx(), rows, asc2.block_num()):\n29:         acc = asc2.reduce_sum(\n30:             asc2.full([1, 64], 0.0, dtype=asc.float32)\n31:         )\n32:         for tile_id in asc2.range(num_tiles):\n33:             col = tile_id * tile_size\n34:             n = tile_size if col + tile_size <= cols else cols - col\n35:             x = asc2.copy_in(\n36:                 x_gm, [row, col], [1, tile_size], real_shape=[1, n]\n37:             )\n38:             xf = x.to(asc.float32)\n39:             acc = acc + asc2.reduce_sum(xf * xf)\n40: \n41:         inv_rms = 1.0 / asc2.sqrt(acc / cols + epsilon)\n42: \n43:         for tile_id in asc2.range(num_tiles):\n44:             col = tile_id * tile_size\n45:             n = tile_size if col + tile_size <= cols else cols - col\n46:             x = asc2.copy_in(\n47:                 x_gm, [row, col], [1, tile_size], real_shape=[1, n]\n48:             )\n49:             gamma = asc2.copy_in(\n50:                 gamma_gm, [col], [tile_size], real_shape=[n]\n51:             )\n52:             y = x.to(asc.float32) * gamma.to(asc.float32) * inv_rms\n53:             asc2.copy_out(\n54:                 y.to(x.dtype),\n55:                 out_gm,\n56:                 [row, col],\n57:                 real_shape=[1, n],\n58:             )\n59: \n60: \n61: @asc2.jit(reuse_alloc=1)\n62: def _rms_norm_kernel(x_ptr: asc.GlobalAddress,\n63:                      gamma_ptr: asc.GlobalAddress,\n64:                      out_ptr: asc.GlobalAddress,\n65:                      rows: int,\n66:                      cols: asc.ConstExpr[int],\n67:                      total_tiles: int,\n68:                      rows_per_tile: asc.ConstExpr[int],\n69:                      epsilon: float):\n70:     x_gm = asc2.global_tensor(x_ptr, [rows, cols])\n71:     gamma_gm = asc2.global_tensor(gamma_ptr, [cols])\n72:     out_gm = asc2.global_tensor(out_ptr, [rows, cols])\n73:     gamma = asc2.copy_in(gamma_gm, [0], [cols])\n74: \n75:     for tile_id in asc2.range(\n76:         asc2.block_idx(), total_tiles, asc2.block_num(), unroll_factor=2\n77:     ):\n78:         row = tile_id * rows_per_tile\n79:         active_rows = (\n80:             rows_per_tile if row + rows_per_tile <= rows else rows - row\n81:         )\n82:         x = asc2.copy_in(\n83:             x_gm,\n84:             [row, 0],\n85:             [rows_per_tile, cols],\n86:             real_shape=[active_rows, cols],\n87:         )\n88:         # pyasc v2's native RMSNorm op accepts f16/f32.  The benchmark's bf16\n89:         # inputs have a wider tolerance, so use an f16 compute path and cast\n90:         # back instead of falling out to a slower scalar reduction.\n91:         if x.dtype == asc.bfloat16:\n92:             y = asc2.rms_norm(\n93:                 x.to(asc.float16), gamma.to(asc.float16), epsilon\n94:             ).to(asc.bfloat16)\n95:         else:\n96:             y = asc2.rms_norm(x, gamma, epsilon)\n97:         asc2.copy_out(\n98:             y,\n99:             out_gm,\n100:             [row, 0],\n101:             real_shape=[active_rows, cols],\n102:         )\n103: \n104: \n105: def _rows_per_tile(cols: int) -> int:\n106:     return max(1, _MAX_TILE_ELEMENTS // cols)\n107: \n108: \n109: def _fallback_tile_size(cols: int) -> int:\n110:     if cols <= 16:\n111:         return 16\n112:     if cols <= 128:\n113:         return 128\n114:     if cols <= 512:\n115:         return 512\n116:     if cols <= 1024:\n117:         return 1024\n118:     if cols <= 2048:\n119:         return 2048\n120:     if cols <= 4096:\n121:         return 4096\n122:     return 8192\n123: \n124: \n125: def rms_norm(x: torch.Tensor, gamma: torch.Tensor,\n126:              epsilon: float = 1e-6) -> torch.Tensor:\n127:     ensure_npu_platform()\n128:     if not x.is_contiguous():\n129:         x = x.contiguous()\n130:     if not gamma.is_contiguous():\n131:         gamma = gamma.contiguous()\n132: \n133:     out = torch.empty_like(x)\n134:     if x.numel() == 0:\n135:         return out\n136: \n137:     cols = x.shape[-1]\n138:     rows = x.numel() // cols\n139:     native_copy_aligned = (cols * x.element_size()) % 32 == 0\n140:     native_fp32_fits_ub = not (\n141:         x.dtype == torch.float32 and cols > _MAX_TILE_ELEMENTS\n142:     )\n143:     if not native_copy_aligned or not native_fp32_fits_ub:\n144:         tile = (\n145:             _MAX_TILE_ELEMENTS\n146:             if not native_fp32_fits_ub\n147:             else _fallback_tile_size(cols)\n148:         )\n149:         num_tiles = asc.ceildiv(cols, tile)\n150:         _rms_norm_fallback_kernel[min(_MAX_CORES, rows)](\n151:             x, gamma, out, rows, cols, num_tiles, tile, float(epsilon)\n152:         )\n153:         return out\n154: \n155:     rows_per_tile = _rows_per_tile(cols)\n156:     total_tiles = asc.ceildiv(rows, rows_per_tile)\n157:     cores = min(_MAX_CORES, total_tiles)\n158:     _rms_norm_kernel[cores](\n159:         x,\n160:         gamma,\n161:         out,\n162:         rows,\n163:         cols,\n164:         total_tiles,\n165:         rows_per_tile,\n166:         float(epsilon),\n167:     )\n168:     return out\n\n(End of file - total 168 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"\"\"\"CANN Bench RMSNorm using pyasc v2's native AscTile RMSNorm op.\"\"\"\n\nimport torch\n\nimport asc\nimport asc2\n\nfrom ._pyasc_runtime import ensure_npu_platform\n\n_MAX_CORES = 72\n_MAX_TILE_ELEMENTS = 4096\n\n\n@asc2.jit(reuse_alloc=1)\ndef _rms_norm_fallback_kernel(x_ptr: asc.GlobalAddress,\n                              gamma_ptr: asc.GlobalAddress,\n                              out_ptr: asc.GlobalAddress,\n                              rows: int,\n                              cols: int,\n                              num_tiles: int,","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/home/aloschilov/workspace/pyasc-skill-stack/integrations/cannbench/submission/cann_bench/rms_norm.py","text":"\"\"\"CANN Bench RMSNorm using pyasc v2's native AscTile RMSNorm op.\"\"\"\n\nimport torch\n\nimport asc\nimport asc2\n\nfrom ._pyasc_runtime import ensure_npu_platform\n\n_MAX_CORES = 72\n_MAX_TILE_ELEMENTS = 4096\n\n\n@asc2.jit(reuse_alloc=1)\ndef _rms_norm_fallback_kernel(x_ptr: asc.GlobalAddress,\n                              gamma_ptr: asc.GlobalAddress,\n                              out_ptr: asc.GlobalAddress,\n                              rows: int,\n                              cols: int,\n                              num_tiles: int,\n                              tile_size: asc.ConstExpr[int],\n                              epsilon: float):\n    \"\"\"Padded two-pass fallback for unaligned D or native FP32 UB overflow.\"\"\"\n    x_gm = asc2.global_tensor(x_ptr, [rows, cols])\n    gamma_gm = asc2.global_tensor(gamma_ptr, [cols])\n    out_gm = asc2.global_tensor(out_ptr, [rows, cols])\n\n    for row in asc2.range(asc2.block_idx(), rows, asc2.block_num()):\n        acc = asc2.reduce_sum(\n            asc2.full([1, 64], 0.0, dtype=asc.float32)\n        )\n        for tile_id in asc2.range(num_tiles):\n            col = tile_id * tile_size\n            n = tile_size if col + tile_size <= cols else cols - col\n            x = asc2.copy_in(\n                x_gm, [row, col], [1, tile_size], real_shape=[1, n]\n            )\n            xf = x.to(asc.float32)\n            acc = acc + asc2.reduce_sum(xf * xf)\n\n        inv_rms = 1.0 / asc2.sqrt(acc / cols + epsilon)\n\n        for tile_id in asc2.range(num_tiles):\n            col = tile_id * tile_size\n            n = tile_size if col + tile_size <= cols else cols - col\n            x = asc2.copy_in(\n                x_gm, [row, col], [1, tile_size], real_shape=[1, n]\n            )\n            gamma = asc2.copy_in(\n                gamma_gm, [col], [tile_size], real_shape=[n]\n            )\n            y = x.to(asc.float32) * gamma.to(asc.float32) * inv_rms\n            asc2.copy_out(\n                y.to(x.dtype),\n                out_gm,\n                [row, col],\n                real_shape=[1, n],\n            )\n\n\n@asc2.jit(reuse_alloc=1)\ndef _rms_norm_kernel(x_ptr: asc.GlobalAddress,\n                     gamma_ptr: asc.GlobalAddress,\n                     out_ptr: asc.GlobalAddress,\n                     rows: int,\n                     cols: asc.ConstExpr[int],\n                     total_tiles: int,\n                     rows_per_tile: asc.ConstExpr[int],\n                     epsilon: float):\n    x_gm = asc2.global_tensor(x_ptr, [rows, cols])\n    gamma_gm = asc2.global_tensor(gamma_ptr, [cols])\n    out_gm = asc2.global_tensor(out_ptr, [rows, cols])\n    gamma = asc2.copy_in(gamma_gm, [0], [cols])\n\n    for tile_id in asc2.range(\n        asc2.block_idx(), total_tiles, asc2.block_num(), unroll_factor=2\n    ):\n        row = tile_id * rows_per_tile\n        active_rows = (\n            rows_per_tile if row + rows_per_tile <= rows else rows - row\n        )\n        x = asc2.copy_in(\n            x_gm,\n            [row, 0],\n            [rows_per_tile, cols],\n            real_shape=[active_rows, cols],\n        )\n        # pyasc v2's native RMSNorm op accepts f16/f32.  The benchmark's bf16\n        # inputs have a wider tolerance, so use an f16 compute path and cast\n        # back instead of falling out to a slower scalar reduction.\n        if x.dtype == asc.bfloat16:\n            y = asc2.rms_norm(\n                x.to(asc.float16), gamma.to(asc.float16), epsilon\n            ).to(asc.bfloat16)\n        else:\n            y = asc2.rms_norm(x, gamma, epsilon)\n        asc2.copy_out(\n            y,\n            out_gm,\n            [row, 0],\n            real_shape=[active_rows, cols],\n        )\n\n\ndef _rows_per_tile(cols: int) -> int:\n    return max(1, _MAX_TILE_ELEMENTS // cols)\n\n\ndef _fallback_tile_size(cols: int) -> int:\n    if cols <= 16:\n        return 16\n    if cols <= 128:\n        return 128\n    if cols <= 512:\n        return 512\n    if cols <= 1024:\n        return 1024\n    if cols <= 2048:\n        return 2048\n    if cols <= 4096:\n        return 4096\n    return 8192\n\n\ndef rms_norm(x: torch.Tensor, gamma: torch.Tensor,\n             epsilon: float = 1e-6) -> torch.Tensor:\n    ensure_npu_platform()\n    if not x.is_contiguous():\n        x = x.contiguous()\n    if not gamma.is_contiguous():\n        gamma = gamma.contiguous()\n\n    out = torch.empty_like(x)\n    if x.numel() == 0:\n        return out\n\n    cols = x.shape[-1]\n    rows = x.numel() // cols\n    native_copy_aligned = (cols * x.element_size()) % 32 == 0\n    native_fp32_fits_ub = not (\n        x.dtype == torch.float32 and cols > _MAX_TILE_ELEMENTS\n    )\n    if not native_copy_aligned or not native_fp32_fits_ub:\n        tile = (\n            _MAX_TILE_ELEMENTS\n            if not native_fp32_fits_ub\n            else _fallback_tile_size(cols)\n        )\n        num_tiles = asc.ceildiv(cols, tile)\n        _rms_norm_fallback_kernel[min(_MAX_CORES, rows)](\n            x, gamma, out, rows, cols, num_tiles, tile, float(epsilon)\n        )\n        return out\n\n    rows_per_tile = _rows_per_tile(cols)\n    total_tiles = asc.ceildiv(rows, rows_per_tile)\n    cores = min(_MAX_CORES, total_tiles)\n    _rms_norm_kernel[cores](\n        x,\n        gamma,\n        out,\n        rows,\n        cols,\n        total_tiles,\n        rows_per_tile,\n        float(epsilon),\n    )\n    return out","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":168,"totalLines":168,"truncated":false}},"title":"integrations/cannbench/submission/cann_bench/rms_norm.py","time":{"start":1788341821946,"end":1788341821962}},"id":"prt_0617aa07e001ubE5QK8oGinalo","sessionID":"ses_f9e8d1600ffeTOnADKxO6TVRTr","messageID":"msg_0617a1e5a001Nc6TkOU2dTjsR2"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788341822316,"sessionID":"ses_f9e8d1600ffeTOnADKxO6TVRTr","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_d27d3a4572284b02a5bd352b","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/aloschilov/workspace/pyasc-skill-stack/integrations/cannbench/submission/cann_bench/sigmoid.py"},"output":"<path>/home/aloschilov/workspace/pyasc-skill-stack/integrations/cannbench/submission/cann_bench/sigmoid.py</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: \"\"\"CANN Bench Sigmoid interface implemented as a pyasc asc2 kernel.\n2: \n3: Kernel design (pyasc-api-patterns Pattern A, grid-stride variant):\n4:   - 1-D flatten; each block strides over tiles so any element count works.\n5:   - Tail tiles handled with ``real_shape`` loads/stores (no host padding).\n6:   - f16/bf16 inputs are promoted to f32 inside the kernel for precision\n7:     (the spec's precision standard expects f32 internal compute).\n8:   - Host selects between two compiled tile sizes: a wide tile (3072) when\n9:     the element count fills all 72 cores, otherwise a narrow tile (1024) to\n10:     maximize core utilization on small shapes.\n11:   - sigmoid(x) = 1 / (1 + e^(-x)); IEEE saturation gives the correct\n12:     limits at extreme inputs (e^inf -> inf -> y=0, e^-inf -> 0 -> y=1).\n13: \"\"\"\n14: \n15: import torch\n16: \n17: import asc\n18: import asc2\n19: \n20: from ._pyasc_runtime import ensure_npu_platform\n21: \n22: _WIDE_TILE = 3072\n23: _NARROW_TILE = 1024\n24: _MAX_CORES = 72\n25: \n26: \n27: @asc2.jit\n28: def _sigmoid_kernel(x_ptr: asc.GlobalAddress, out_ptr: asc.GlobalAddress,\n29:                     size: int, num_tiles: int, tile_size: asc.ConstExpr[int]):\n30:     x_gm = asc2.global_tensor(x_ptr, [size])\n31:     out_gm = asc2.global_tensor(out_ptr, [size])\n32:     for t in asc2.range(asc2.block_idx(), num_tiles, asc2.block_num(),\n33:                         unroll_factor=2):\n34:         off = t * tile_size\n35:         n = tile_size if off + tile_size <= size else size - off\n36:         x = asc2.copy_in(x_gm, [off], [tile_size], real_shape=[n])\n37:         xf = x.to(asc.float32)\n38:         y = asc2.div(1.0, asc2.exp(-xf) + 1.0)\n39:         asc2.copy_out(y.to(x.dtype), out_gm, [off], real_shape=[n])\n40: \n41: \n42: def sigmoid(x: torch.Tensor) -> torch.Tensor:\n43:     \"\"\"Element-wise sigmoid of an NPU tensor via a pyasc asc2 kernel.\"\"\"\n44:     ensure_npu_platform()\n45:     if not x.is_contiguous():\n46:         x = x.contiguous()\n47:     out = torch.empty_like(x)\n48:     size = x.numel()\n49:     if size == 0:\n50:         return out\n51:     if size >= _MAX_CORES * _WIDE_TILE:\n52:         num_tiles = asc.ceildiv(size, _WIDE_TILE)\n53:         cores = min(_MAX_CORES, num_tiles)\n54:         _sigmoid_kernel[cores](x, out, size, num_tiles, _WIDE_TILE)\n55:     else:\n56:         num_tiles = asc.ceildiv(size, _NARROW_TILE)\n57:         cores = min(_MAX_CORES, num_tiles)\n58:         _sigmoid_kernel[cores](x, out, size, num_tiles, _NARROW_TILE)\n59:     return out\n\n(End of file - total 59 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"\"\"\"CANN Bench Sigmoid interface implemented as a pyasc asc2 kernel.\n\nKernel design (pyasc-api-patterns Pattern A, grid-stride variant):\n  - 1-D flatten; each block strides over tiles so any element count works.\n  - Tail tiles handled with ``real_shape`` loads/stores (no host padding).\n  - f16/bf16 inputs are promoted to f32 inside the kernel for precision\n    (the spec's precision standard expects f32 internal compute).\n  - Host selects between two compiled tile sizes: a wide tile (3072) when\n    the element count fills all 72 cores, otherwise a narrow tile (1024) to\n    maximize core utilization on small shapes.\n  - sigmoid(x) = 1 / (1 + e^(-x)); IEEE saturation gives the correct\n    limits at extreme inputs (e^inf -> inf -> y=0, e^-inf -> 0 -> y=1).\n\"\"\"\n\nimport torch\n\nimport asc\nimport asc2\n\nfrom ._pyasc_runtime import ensure_npu_platform","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/home/aloschilov/workspace/pyasc-skill-stack/integrations/cannbench/submission/cann_bench/sigmoid.py","text":"\"\"\"CANN Bench Sigmoid interface implemented as a pyasc asc2 kernel.\n\nKernel design (pyasc-api-patterns Pattern A, grid-stride variant):\n  - 1-D flatten; each block strides over tiles so any element count works.\n  - Tail tiles handled with ``real_shape`` loads/stores (no host padding).\n  - f16/bf16 inputs are promoted to f32 inside the kernel for precision\n    (the spec's precision standard expects f32 internal compute).\n  - Host selects between two compiled tile sizes: a wide tile (3072) when\n    the element count fills all 72 cores, otherwise a narrow tile (1024) to\n    maximize core utilization on small shapes.\n  - sigmoid(x) = 1 / (1 + e^(-x)); IEEE saturation gives the correct\n    limits at extreme inputs (e^inf -> inf -> y=0, e^-inf -> 0 -> y=1).\n\"\"\"\n\nimport torch\n\nimport asc\nimport asc2\n\nfrom ._pyasc_runtime import ensure_npu_platform\n\n_WIDE_TILE = 3072\n_NARROW_TILE = 1024\n_MAX_CORES = 72\n\n\n@asc2.jit\ndef _sigmoid_kernel(x_ptr: asc.GlobalAddress, out_ptr: asc.GlobalAddress,\n                    size: int, num_tiles: int, tile_size: asc.ConstExpr[int]):\n    x_gm = asc2.global_tensor(x_ptr, [size])\n    out_gm = asc2.global_tensor(out_ptr, [size])\n    for t in asc2.range(asc2.block_idx(), num_tiles, asc2.block_num(),\n                        unroll_factor=2):\n        off = t * tile_size\n        n = tile_size if off + tile_size <= size else size - off\n        x = asc2.copy_in(x_gm, [off], [tile_size], real_shape=[n])\n        xf = x.to(asc.float32)\n        y = asc2.div(1.0, asc2.exp(-xf) + 1.0)\n        asc2.copy_out(y.to(x.dtype), out_gm, [off], real_shape=[n])\n\n\ndef sigmoid(x: torch.Tensor) -> torch.Tensor:\n    \"\"\"Element-wise sigmoid of an NPU tensor via a pyasc asc2 kernel.\"\"\"\n    ensure_npu_platform()\n    if not x.is_contiguous():\n        x = x.contiguous()\n    out = torch.empty_like(x)\n    size = x.numel()\n    if size == 0:\n        return out\n    if size >= _MAX_CORES * _WIDE_TILE:\n        num_tiles = asc.ceildiv(size, _WIDE_TILE)\n        cores = min(_MAX_CORES, num_tiles)\n        _sigmoid_kernel[cores](x, out, size, num_tiles, _WIDE_TILE)\n    else:\n        num_tiles = asc.ceildiv(size, _NARROW_TILE)\n        cores = min(_MAX_CORES, num_tiles)\n        _sigmoid_kernel[cores](x, out, size, num_tiles, _NARROW_TILE)\n    return out","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":59,"totalLines":59,"truncated":false}},"title":"integrations/cannbench/submission/cann_bench/sigmoid.py","time":{"start":1788341822307,"end":1788341822315}},"id":"prt_0617aa2490010aGwNPDEoCCZaa","sessionID":"ses_f9e8d1600ffeTOnADKxO6TVRTr","messageID":"msg_0617a1e5a001Nc6TkOU2dTjsR2"}}
